# The deploy builds in /home/deploy/list-wheel with `COPY . .`, so everything
# not listed here lands in the build stage's layer in the box's image cache and
# invalidates that layer when it changes. The serving stage copies only
# dist/list-wheel/browser forward, so the served image is clean either way; this
# keeps the context and that layer small and the layer stable across edits to
# files the build never reads.
#
# From .gitignore: the compiled output and the Angular cache. A checkout on the
# box has neither, but a local `docker build` after an `ng build` would send a
# stale dist/ that the build stage then overwrites anyway.
dist
.angular
# `npm ci` in the build stage installs a clean tree. A host node_modules sent
# with the context would be copied over it by `COPY . .`.
node_modules
coverage

.git
.github
.gitignore
.vscode

*.md
*.excalidraw

Dockerfile
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore
